----  1 agent agent     265 Nov 17 13:27 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\n-rw-------  1 agent agent     279 Nov 17 13:27 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\n-rw-------  1 agent agent    2906 Nov 17 13:29 reference_retrieval.log\n-rw-------  1 agent agent    6646 Nov 17 14:02 references.bib\n-rw-r--r--  1 agent agent    1695 Nov 17 14:07 references.bib.prov.json\n-rw-------  1 agent agent   24123 Nov 17 14:02 references_provenance.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 agent agent    1641 Nov 17 14:07 references_provenance.json.prov.json\nlrwxrwxrwx  1 agent agent      16 Nov 17 13:22 results -> ../investigation\n-rw-r--r--  1 agent agent    5485 Nov 17 14:02 retrieve_paper_references.py\ndrwx------  2 agent agent    4096 Nov 17 14:40 revisions\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 agent agent    4096 Nov 17 14:40 scientific-evidence\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 agent agent    4096 Nov 17 13:44 source_evidence\n-rw-r--r--  1 agent agent    2429 Nov 17 13:59 source_evidence_manifest.json\n-rw-------  1 agent agent     265 Nov 17 13:38 strategy_validation_feedback.json\n-rw-------  1 agent agent     271 Nov 17 13:38 strategy_validation_feedback.md\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 agent agent    4096 Nov 17 13:44 tables\nlrwxrwxrwx  1 agent agent       7 Nov 17 13:22 task -> ../task\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 agent agent    4096 Nov 17 14:00 template_evidence\n-rw-r--r--  1 agent agent    8215 Nov 17 13:41 template_provenance.json\n-rw-------  1 agent agent    3915 Nov 17 14:40 validation_feedback.json\n-rw-------  1 agent agent    3049 Nov 17 14:40 validation_feedback.md\n-rw-------  1 agent agent   21749 Nov 17 14:40 validation_report.json\n=== VENUE.md\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\n=== validation_feedback.json\n{\n  \"agentic_evidence_audit\": {\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"finding_count\": 1,\n    \"findings\": [\n      {\n        \"claim\": \"Effective count equals (sum w)^2/sum(w^2).\",\n        \"evidence\": \"paper.tex:122 omits the floor; source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:177 applies it during prediction, and source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:194 applies it during calibration; the prediction path calls this correction at source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:315.\",\n        \"fix\": \"Change the manuscript equation to (sum w)^2/max(sum(w^2),1e-12), disclose the denominator floor, and qualify the concentration-only interpretation when that floor is active.\",\n        \"id\": \"method-effective-count-floor\",\n        \"issue\": \"The implementation floors the denominator at 1e-12. This changes shrinkage when squared weights sum below that floor, even when total weight exceeds the separately disclosed cutoff.\",\n        \"section\": \"Method: Cross-fitted local residual transfer\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"summary\": \"Retained results and qualification are supported, but the residual-shrinkage equation does not match the evaluated implementation.\",\n    \"verdict\": \"fail\"\n  },\n  \"evidence_validation\": {\n    \"bundle_path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/scientific-evidence\",\n    \"bundle_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"dangling\": [],\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"paper_token_count\": 204,\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"anchored_references\": 79,\n      \"dangling_references\": 0,\n      \"manifests_checked\": 15,\n      \"resolved_references\": 125,\n      \"total_references\": 204\n    },\n    \"verification_report_path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json\"\n  },\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-17T14:40:16.093565+00:00\",\n  \"hard_errors\": [\n    \"agentic evidence audit failed: see work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json and work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md\",\n    \"figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for budget_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for history_structure_controls\"\n  ],\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"page_validation\": {\n    \"body_pages\": null,\n    \"checked\": false,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"exclude_references\": false,\n    \"last_body_page_counted\": null,\n    \"last_body_page_fill_ratio\": null,\n    \"last_body_page_number\": null,\n    \"max_body_pages\": null,\n    \"min_body_pages\": null,\n    \"min_last_body_page_fill_ratio\": null,\n    \"paper_format\": null,\n    \"reference_start_page\": null,\n    \"supplement_pages\": 0,\n    \"supplement_start_page\": null,\n    \"total_pages\": null\n  },\n  \"paper_dir\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper\",\n  \"pdf_path\": null,\n  \"soft_warnings\": [\n    \"figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\",\n    \"figures[2] PNG width too small: 1485 < 2400\",\n    \"figures[2] PNG height too small: 585 < 700\"\n  ],\n  \"supplementary_information_validation\": {\n    \"appendix_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"clearpage_present\": true,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"heading_present\": true,\n    \"placed_after_references\": true,\n    \"pre_bibliography_clearpage_present\": true,\n    \"rendered_checked\": false,\n    \"rendered_heading_present\": false,\n    \"rendered_visible_character_count\": 0,\n    \"substantive_element_count\": 9,\n    \"visible_character_count\": 9617\n  }\n}=== validation_feedback.md\n# Paper validation feedback\n\n- generated_at: 2026-11-17T14:40:16.093565+00:00\n- paper_dir: `work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper`\n- ok: `False`\n\n## Hard errors\n- agentic evidence audit failed: see work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json and work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md\n- figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for budget_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for history_structure_controls\n\n## Supplementary Information validation\n- appendix_present: `True`\n- heading_present: `True`\n- placed_after_references: `True`\n- pre_bibliography_clearpage_present: `True`\n- clearpage_present: `True`\n- visible_character_count: `9617`\n- substantive_element_count: `9`\n- rendered_checked: `False`\n- rendered_heading_present: `False`\n- rendered_visible_character_count: `0`\n\n## Evidence validation\n- bundle_path: `work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/scientific-evidence`\n- bundle_present: `True`\n- verification_report: `work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json`\n- total_references: `204`\n- resolved_references: `125`\n- anchored_references: `79`\n- dangling_references: `0`\n- manifests_checked: `15`\n\n## Agentic evidence audit\n- checked: `True`\n- verdict: `fail`\n- finding_count: `1`\n- summary: Retained results and qualification are supported, but the residual-shrinkage equation does not match the evaluated implementation.\n\n### Audit findings to fix\n- `method-effective-count-floor` (Method: Cross-fitted local residual transfer): The implementation floors the denominator at 1e-12. This changes shrinkage when squared weights sum below that floor, even when total weight exceeds the separately disclosed cutoff.\n  - claim: Effective count equals (sum w)^2/sum(w^2).\n  - evidence: paper.tex:122 omits the floor; source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:177 applies it during prediction, and source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:194 applies it during calibration; the prediction path calls this correction at source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:315.\n  - requested_fix: Change the manuscript equation to (sum w)^2/max(sum(w^2),1e-12), disclose the denominator floor, and qualify the concentration-only interpretation when that floor is active.\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1485 < 2400\n- figures[2] PNG height too small: 585 < 700\n=== draft_reference_gaps.md\n# Draft Reference Gap Analysis\n\n**Status:** `no_gaps`\n\nThe draft directly cites its related-work families and supports its methodological positioning with existing references, so no paragraph-specific citation gap warrants targeted post-draft retrieval.\n\n## Grounded Review\n\nReviewed `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, `references_provenance.json`, `claims_grounding.json`, `paper_data.json`, `paper_strategy.json`, and `global_memory_summary.md`. Used the memory summary only as qualitative context. Checked citation-key coverage and provenance, and inspected relevant already-retained abstracts locally; no external search or retrieval was performed.\n\n## Coverage Decisions\n\n- **Related Work — Reducing evaluation and predicting performance** (`paper.tex:43`): MTEB, item-level evaluation reduction, and low-dimensional cross-benchmark prediction have direct citations to `MTEB`, `TinyBenchmarks`, `MetaBench`, `ObservationalScaling`, and `Sloth`. The paragraph explicitly distinguishes acquisition granularity and generative-model evidence from the present embedding experiment; it does not claim these works were tested as baselines.\n- **Related Work — Incomplete matrices and local prediction** (`paper.tex:46`): Factorization, neighborhood methods, probabilistic uncertainty, implicit-feedback semantics, matrix completion, and median-based prediction are directly cited. The draft limits these connections to antecedents rather than importing recovery guarantees or claiming component novelty.\n- **Related Work — Design and empirical inference** (`paper.tex:49`): Experimental design, active learning, ridge regularization, missingness, bootstrap inference, and dependence already have direct citations. The manuscript separately specifies and qualifies its actual acquisition surrogate and resampling construction.\n- **Introduction and Method** (`paper.tex:19`, `paper.tex:52`): The introduction's benchmark context is cited, and its global/local rationale is developed through the cited related work. Estimator equations, calibration rules, and acquisition algebra describe the studied implementation or explicit derivations, not uncited claims of established superiority or calibrated uncertainty.\n\nAll 25 unique cited keys resolve in the bibliography and provenance; every provenance entry points to an existing local consulted-content file. This supports the coverage assessment, not a claim of exhaustive literature review.\n\n## Exclusions and Recommendation\n\nQuantitative outcomes and protocol details are grounded in the retained data and claim mappings, so they do not justify literature retrieval. The five experimental comparators are explicitly defined evaluator configurations rather than unattributed named external methods. Missing ablations, genuinely missing-cell validation, temporal transfer, and broader generalization are acknowledged evidence limitations; additional citations cannot supply those experiments.\n\n**Missing literatures:** none identified that warrant retrieval for the current narrative.\n\n**Rewrite targets:** none. Skip the targeted post-draft retrieval pass; preserve the current story and its limitations. No changes were made to the manuscript, bibliography, or reference provenance.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
