{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md; cat paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json; cat figure_manifest.json; sed -n '1,220p' check_paper_locally.py; sed -n '1,225p' build_claims.py\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evaluations, failures, and next hypotheses during agent runs.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nKeep durable run memory so idea evolution and program evidence are never lost between steps.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- At run start to initialize memory.\n- After every meaningful step (`idea`, `edit`, `evaluate`, `verify`, `paper`, `draft`).\n- Immediately after every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair.\n\n# What to do\n1. Initialize `./memory.md` if missing with these section headers:\n- `# Memory Log`\n- `## Context`\n- `## Idea Discoveries`\n- `## Program Evaluations`\n- `## Failures / Regressions`\n- `## Next Hypotheses`\n2. Also initialize global files if missing:\n- `./global_memory/memory.md`\n- `./global_memory/memory.jsonl`\n3. Never delete or rewrite prior entries; append only.\n4. For each appended entry, include:\n- timestamp\n- step type\n- change/discovery summary\n- concrete evidence\n- next action\n5. After every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair, append a `Program Evaluations` entry that includes:\n- `program_<idx>`\n- `combined_score`\n- `correct`\n- rubric pass/fail summary\n- `next_recommendation`\n6. For regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly\nto the required markdown and JSONL files. Preserve all existing content. When command\nexecution is available, prefer the helper for deterministic dual-write:\n- script: detect the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\nMEMORY_HELPER=\"$(find ./.claude ./.codex ./.cursor ./.opencode ./.gemini ./.pi -path '*/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py' -print -quit 2>/dev/null)\"\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" \\\n  --global-memory-md \"./global_memory/memory.md\" \\\n  --global-memory-jsonl \"./global_memory/memory.jsonl\" \\\n  --event-json '{\"step\":\"evaluate\",\"scope\":\"attempt\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"evidence\":\"...\",\"next_action\":\"...\",\"attempt_id\":\"{{ATTEMPT_ID}}\",\"idea_id\":\"{{IDEA_ID}}\",\"program_id\":\"program_2\",\"metrics\":{\"combined_score\":2.54,\"correct\":true}}'\n```\n9. JSONL event schema (required keys):\n- `timestamp` (auto-filled if omitted)\n- `step` (`idea|edit|evaluate|verify|paper|draft|final|conclusions_skip`)\n- `scope` (`idea|attempt|paper|campaign`)\n- `summary`\n- `evidence`\n- `next_action`\n- optional: `idea_id`, `attempt_id`, `program_id`, `metrics`, `rubrics`, `tags`\n\n10. Update distilled conclusions (`conclusions.md`).\n**Purpose.** `conclusions.md` is a *forward-looking guide* for the next worker (or your future self in a later cycle). Its job is to help readers (a) focus their effort on directions you've found promising, and (b) avoid spending compute on directions you've already shown to be unpromising. Each sentence should either point at a lead worth pursuing or warn against a dead end, framed so a researcher who has not read your `memory.md` can still act on it. Avoid chronology, restate-of-results, and post-mortem narration — those belong in `memory.md`. Conclusions are the synthesis layer that makes other workers' next cycles more efficient.\n\n**When.** After every memory-append in the cycle (idea / edit / evaluate / verify / paper / final), evaluate whether `conclusions.md` should be updated.\n\n**Update gate (the only valid triggers).**\n- (a) cycle **contradicts** an existing sentence → rewrite that sentence.\n- (b) cycle opens a **new category** not yet covered → add a sentence.\n- (c) cycle **flips a Do/Don't** recommendation → flip it.\n- (d) cycle **meaningfully refines** an existing sentence — narrows the conditions under which a rule holds, broadens its applicability to a config it wasn't known to apply to, sharpens a tentative claim into a confident one, or adds a qualifier the prior phrasing didn't cover → edit the sentence to incorporate the refinement. Simple re-confirmation in the same regime is **not** sufficient; you must identify the refinement dimension (narrow / broaden / sharpen / qualify) in `--gate-reason`.\n- otherwise → **keep**, do not invoke the helper.\n\n**Format constraints.** Single paragraph. ≤300 words. No blank lines (`\\n\\n`). Avoid detailed numerical figures — use qualitative thresholds (e.g. \"low LR\", \"small batch\") instead of precise floats like `LR=0.205`.\n\n**Update mechanism.** When execution is unavailable, apply the same validation rules\nand update the conclusions files directly with read/edit/write tools. When execution\nis available, use this helper invocation:\n```bash\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" --write-conclusions \\\n  --conclusions-md \"{{CONCLUSIONS_MD_FILE}}\" \\\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl \"{{CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_FILE}}\" \\\n  --cycle-index {{CYCLE_INDEX}} \\\n  --worker-index {{WORKER_INDEX}} \\\n  --gate-trigger <a|b|c|d> \\\n  --gate-reason \"<one sentence; for (d) name the dimension>\" \\\n  --conclusions-text \"<the full new paragraph>\"\n```\n\n**Pre-flight self-check.** Before invoking the helper, count words (`len(paragraph.split())`) and confirm ≤300, and that the paragraph contains no blank line. Most validation rejections can be avoided here.\n\n**Retry budget — exactly 3 attempts per cycle.** On non-zero exit, read the stderr error, shorten the paragraph (drop the least-decisive sentence, merge two related sentences, or remove qualifiers), and retry. After **3 total attempts** with no success, the update is **discarded** for this cycle: do not retry further, do not write the rejected text anywhere, and append a single memory event with `step=\"conclusions_skip\"` whose `summary` names the last validation error. Underlying findings are not lost — they are already durable in `memory.md`.\n\n**Always log the gate decision.** Inside the regular memory append for the cycle, include `gate=<updated|kept|skipped>; trigger=<a|b|c|d|none>; reason=<one sentence>` in the entry's `summary` or `tags`. Use `skipped` only after the 3-attempt budget is exhausted.\n\n# Example evaluation entry\n```markdown\n### 2026-02-13T16:58:00Z | step=evaluate\n- program: program_3\n- combined_score: 2.54\n- correct: true\n- rubrics: uses_restarts=pass, constraint_optimization=pass, score_threshold=fail\n- evidence: late-stage overlap still visible in stdout trace\n- next_recommendation: raise late-stage overlap penalty and diversify restart seeds\n```\n{\n  \"audit_json_path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/paper_evidence_audit.json\",\n  \"audit_markdown_path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md\",\n  \"finding_count\": 1,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Effective count equals (sum w)^2/sum(w^2).\",\n      \"evidence\": \"paper.tex:122 omits the floor; source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:177 applies it during prediction, and source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:194 applies it during calibration; the prediction path calls this correction at source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:315.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Change the manuscript equation to (sum w)^2/max(sum(w^2),1e-12), disclose the denominator floor, and qualify the concentration-only interpretation when that floor is active.\",\n      \"id\": \"method-effective-count-floor\",\n      \"issue\": \"The implementation floors the denominator at 1e-12. This changes shrinkage when squared weights sum below that floor, even when total weight exceeds the separately disclosed cutoff.\",\n      \"section\": \"Method: Cross-fitted local residual transfer\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-17T14:40:15.989410+00:00\",\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"raw_output_path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/paper/paper_evidence_audit_raw.txt\",\n  \"summary\": \"Retained results and qualification are supported, but the residual-shrinkage equation does not match the evaluated implementation.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\"\n}{\n  \"figures\": [\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        5,\n        5\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.8,\n      \"figure_id\": \"method_overview\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 9,\n        \"ticks\": 9,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 36,\n      \"n_panels\": 2,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 1,\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/method_overview.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"prompt_log_path\": \"figures/method_overview.prompts.json\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        2,\n        2\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        4,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.8,\n      \"figure_id\": \"budget_comparison\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"line\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 9,\n        \"ticks\": 9,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 36,\n      \"n_panels\": 2,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/budget_comparison.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/budget_comparison.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        4,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        3\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.8,\n      \"figure_id\": \"history_structure_controls\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"scatter\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 9,\n        \"ticks\": 9,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 0.9,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 36,\n      \"n_panels\": 1,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 1,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/history_structure_controls.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/history_structure_controls.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        3\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport subprocess\n\nimport jsonschema\nimport pymupdf\n\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"@evidence[[paper.tex]]\n    @evidence[[figure_manifest.json]]\n    @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation]]\n    \"\"\"\n    report = dict(checks={}, canonical_limitations=[])\n    manifest = json.loads(Path('figure_manifest.json').read_text())\n    schema = json.loads(Path('.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json').read_text())\n    jsonschema.validate(manifest, schema)\n    report['checks']['figure_schema'] = True\n    strategy = json.loads(Path('paper_strategy.json').read_text())\n    specifications = {entry['figure_id']: entry for entry in strategy['figure_specs']}\n    tex = Path('paper.tex').read_text()\n    referenced = re.findall(r'\\\\includegraphics(?:\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\{([^}]+)\\}', tex)\n    for figure in manifest['figures']:\n        spec = specifications[figure['figure_id']]\n        assert figure['n_panels'] <= spec['max_panels']\n        assert figure['panels_per_row'] <= spec['max_panels_per_row']\n        assert max(figure['categories_per_panel']) <= spec['max_categories_per_panel']\n        assert max(figure['series_per_panel']) <= spec['max_series_per_panel']\n        for key in ['path_pdf', 'path_png', 'prompt_log_path']:\n            if figure.get(key):\n                assert Path(figure[key]).is_file()\n        used = figure.get('path_pdf') or figure['path_png']\n        assert used in referenced\n        if figure['generator'] == 'matplotlib':\n            assert figure['estimated_min_rendered_font_pt'] >= 8.5\n    assert len(referenced) == len(manifest['figures'])\n    report['checks']['figure_assets_and_strategy_budgets'] = True\n    report['concept_render_status'] = 'rendered' if Path('.concept_figure_complete').exists() else 'placeholder; orchestrator rendering pending by contract'\n    report['canonical_limitations'].append('Canonical validate_figures.py cannot import the unavailable src.orchestrator package; local JSON Schema, asset, density and placement checks are reported separately.')\n    pdf = pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\n    page_texts = [page.get_text() for page in pdf]\n    references = next(index for index, text in enumerate(page_texts) if re.search(r'(?m)^REFERENCES\\s*$', text))\n    assert 8 <= references <= 9\n    blocks = [block for block in pdf[references - 1].get_text('blocks') if block[0] >= 100 and block[1] >= 75 and block[3] < 745]\n    bottom = max(block[3] for block in blocks)\n    occupancy = (bottom - 80) / 648\n    assert references != 8 or occupancy >= .75\n    report['checks']['body_pages'] = references\n    report['checks']['last_body_page_geometric_vertical_fraction'] = occupancy\n    report['checks']['total_pages'] = len(pdf)\n    visible = '\\n'.join(page_texts)\n    forbidden = r'\\b(?:idea|ideas|program|programs|attempt|attempts|eligible|worker_01|worker_02|combined_score|rubric)\\b'\n    assert not re.search(forbidden, visible, re.I)\n    assert 'Anonymous authors' in visible\n    assert not re.search(r'(?mi)^\\s*(?:acknowledg\\w*|funding)\\s*$', visible)\n    report['checks']['visible_language_and_anonymity'] = True\n    si_path = Path('.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py')\n    specification = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('rendered_si', si_path)\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(specification)\n    specification.loader.exec_module(module)\n    rendered = subprocess.run(['pdftotext', '-layout', 'paper.pdf', '-'], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\n    assert not module.validate_rendered_supplementary_information(rendered.stdout.split('\\f'))\n    report['checks']['rendered_supplement'] = True\n    for stem in ['budget_details', 'seed_details']:\n        assert Path('tables/' + stem + '.tex').read_text().strip() in tex\n    report['checks']['embedded_supplement_tables_equal_generated_tables'] = True\n    for target, pointer in re.findall(r'@evidence\\[\\[([^#\\]]+)#(/[^\\]]*)\\]\\]', tex):\n        if target.endswith('.json'):\n            value = json.loads(Path(target).read_text())\n            for part in pointer[1:].split('/'):\n                part = part.replace('~1', '/').replace('~0', '~')\n                value = value[int(part)] if isinstance(value, list) else value[part]\n    report['checks']['manuscript_json_pointers_resolve'] = True\n    log = Path('paper.log').read_text()\n    assert 'undefined' not in log.lower()\n    assert 'Overfull' not in log\n    report['checks']['no_unresolved_tex_references_or_overfull_boxes'] = True\n    bibkeys = re.findall(r'@\\w+\\{([^,]+),', Path('references.bib').read_text())\n    assert 25 <= len(bibkeys) <= 30\n    report['checks']['reference_count'] = len(bibkeys)\n    claims = json.loads(Path('claims_grounding.json').read_text())\n    report['checks']['mapped_claims'] = len(claims['claims'])\n    gate = subprocess.run(['python3', '.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py', 'recorder', '--paper-dir', '.', '--fls', 'paper.fls'], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    report['canonical_compile_input_gate'] = dict(passed=gate.returncode == 0, message=(gate.stdout + gate.stderr).strip())\n    if gate.returncode:\n        report['canonical_limitations'].append('Canonical recorder gate rejects Debian system texmf.cnf symlink. Direct compilation and independent resolved-path dependency checks succeeded; canonical gate is not reported as passed.')\n        for line in Path('paper.fls').read_text().splitlines():\n            if line.startswith('INPUT '):\n                path = Path(line[6:]).resolve()\n                assert path.is_relative_to(Path.cwd()) or any(path.is_relative_to(Path(root)) for root in ['/usr/share/texlive', '/etc/texmf', '/var/lib/texmf']), str(path)\n    report['checks']['resolved_compilation_inputs_within_workspace_or_system_tex_roots'] = True\n    Path('local_validation_report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n    for index in [0, 1, references - 1, references + 2]:\n        pdf[index].get_pixmap(matrix=pymupdf.Matrix(1.3, 1.3)).save('/tmp/manuscript_page_' + str(index + 1) + '.png')\n    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation]]\n    @evidence[[references_provenance.json#/references]]\n    \"\"\"\n    claims = []\n\n    def add(text, sources, locations=None):\n        claim = dict(claim=text, source_ids=sources, citation_keys=[])\n        if locations:\n            claim['source_locations'] = locations\n        claims.append(claim)\n\n    episodes = ['final.evidence.episodes']\n    implementation = ['result.best_correct_score']\n    add('Final evaluation completed and qualified; qualification is not evidence of universal validity or superiority.', ['final.qualification.status', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.correct'])\n    add('The final frozen MTEB plane has 126 rows and 135 task/subset columns, not independent benchmark suites; results revision is 6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383.', episodes, ['source_evidence/resources/final/manifest.json:1', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:715'])\n    add('English text-only main-score extraction preserves bounded noncorrelations and maps correlations by (x+1)/2; task-definition revision 5a83aafe4e7140d0606b96f59448c704f31dbf76, global support 32 and row support 12 are manifest rules.', episodes, ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:685', 'source_evidence/resources/final/manifest.json:1'])\n    add('History/test alias and normalized content separation are checked; family holdout additionally separates heuristic family labels. This does not certify true ancestry or pretraining independence.', episodes, ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:715'])\n    add('A shuffled approximately two-thirds reservoir, cut at least eight, is disjoint from a sealed target set fixed across budgets and methods; only observed cells are retrospectively evaluated.', episodes, ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:851'])\n    add('Rank-four ridge ALS with ridge 0.1, fifty sweeps and Gaussian factor initialization SD 0.1 fits observed entries only; historical means remain fixed.', implementation + episodes, ['source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:363', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:920'])\n    add('Ridge conditioning and the all-column integrated-variance acquisition formula describe the evaluated source. The rank-one algebra is a surrogate reduction, not an MAE or calibrated posterior guarantee; selection is independent of revealed values.', implementation, ['source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:395'])\n    add('Donor-excluded auxiliary predictions yield residuals only for observed donor targets; shared-anchor kernel weights are multiplied by overlap fraction, use a 0.025 scale floor, and vanish at zero overlap.', implementation, ['source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:51', 'source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:97', 'source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:145'])\n    add('Weighted median residual correction uses effective-count shrinkage, excludes queried columns, clips to [0,1], and leaves the base unchanged below total-weight threshold 1e-12 or at zero blend.', implementation, ['source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:164', 'source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:300'])\n    add('History-only nested calibration uses two validation folds and two donor folds, at most 16 validation rows, 128 donors, 12 auxiliary sweeps, and pool cap min(512,max(64,floor(196608/N))).', implementation, ['source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:200'])\n    add('Calibration grid h={0.35,0.75,1.5}, tau={4,16}, alpha={0,0.25,0.5,1} includes exact zero fallback; historical finite-cell pooling differs from fixed-target outer row averaging.', implementation, ['source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:200'])\n    add('ALS arithmetic cost O(E r^2+(M+N)r^3) per sweep and donor-by-column residual storage are direct algebraic consequences of the inspected dense-solve loops, not measured runtime or novel theory.', implementation, ['source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:51', 'source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:363'])\n    add('Five final references are column mean, query mean, random-query low-rank, variance-query low-rank, and linear ridge; query policies differ and centered missing entries in linear ridge are zero-filled.', episodes, ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:870'])\n    add('Constant history preserves masks and replaces observed values by column means. Column shifting rolls each value/mask pair by an independent nonzero offset, preserving per-column observed multisets; controls match model holdout.', episodes, ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:808', 'source_evidence/resources/final/plan.json:1'])\n    add('Budgets 1,2,4,8 use nested prefixes; seeds 6841,8089,9011; history/test sizes 94/32 except final family split 93/33; six primary condition/seed averages have equal weight.', episodes, ['source_evidence/resources/final/plan.json:1', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:970'])\n    add('Aggregate MAE 0.040807843083862115, RMSE 0.06432104648676243, strongest aggregate baseline 0.045249969215420516, gain 0.004442126131558401, relative reduction 9.816860008%.', ['final.metric.mae','final.metric.rmse','final.metric.baseline_mae','final.metric.delta_best_baseline'], ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('All six estimators and both holdouts in Table 1, the complete budget table, and seed table reproduce retained episode arrays; the studied configuration has lower aggregate MAE in each holdout than every reference.', episodes, ['derived_results.json:1','tables/main_comparison.tex:1','tables/budget_details.tex:1','tables/seed_details.tex:1'])\n    add('Studied MAE model/family=0.038312665669/0.043303020499 versus linear ridge 0.045116500008/0.045383438423; partitions differ, so no causal effect of family membership is inferred.', episodes, ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('Studied seed MAEs 0.038496586319,0.041126033629,0.042800909303 (sample SD 0.002169731091); linear-ridge seed MAEs 0.041657905965,0.045940218194,0.048151783488. Seeds share source data.', episodes, ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('Primary budget MAEs 0.045233341978,0.042208509062,0.039639061083,0.036150460213 decrease over k=1,2,4,8. Each holdout seed-mean curve decreases, without per-model monotonicity or sufficient-budget claims.', ['final.metric.mae_k1','final.metric.mae_k2','final.metric.mae_k4','final.metric.mae_k8'] + episodes, ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('At eight queries studied model/family errors are 0.034476748972/0.037824171454, versus ridge 0.039273276354/0.039840694780.', episodes, ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('Paired component resampling uses 400 draws and RNG 424242; quantiles .005/.995 for each of five baselines precede separate minima of lower and upper bounds. These are not a conventional single-comparator interval.', episodes + ['final.metric.gain_ci_low','final.metric.gain_ci_high'], ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:999','derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('Reported bound minima [0.0021032442082077377,0.009199712663056218] are reconstructed exactly; all baseline-specific intervals in the supplement come from the same retained paired arrays.', ['final.metric.gain_ci_low','final.metric.gain_ci_high'] + episodes, ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('Matched model-holdout intact MAE 0.038312665669 rises to 0.064367113099 under constant history and 0.068569520893 under column shifts; shifted column mean is 0.064367113099 and variance low-rank 0.070913935972. The method loses to column mean under shifts.', ['final.metric.constant_control_mae','final.metric.permuted_control_mae'] + episodes, ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('Constant-history column means and all centered historical linear references equal the studied sealed-target MAE; controls do not isolate any component.', episodes, ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('All-unqueried changing-target diagnostic MAEs A/B/C/D=0.036645358811/0.042420107742/0.065275510462/0.063523296739; not a common-target comparison.', episodes, ['derived_results.json:1'])\n    add('Reset replay query sequences matched and maximum absolute prediction difference was zero; diagnostics do not certify all possible leakage checks.', ['final.metric.reset_max_abs_delta','final.qualification.outcome'], ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:976'])\n    add('No matched final residual-off, unconditional-residual, donor-only, support-gating, temporal, cross-leaderboard or missingness-stratified result is available; sequential development does not isolate causal components.', episodes + implementation, ['source_evidence/selected/src/program.py:200'])\n    add('Two development configurations have numeric results; one support-gating evaluation has no retained numeric performance and an unknown failure cause. It is not a measured loss.', ['result.total_attempts','result.total_evaluated_programs'], ['paper_data.json:1'])\n    add('Manifest records current CC0-1.0 evidence and Apache-2.0 metadata but absence of a results license at the pinned snapshot; historical licensing remains qualified.', episodes, ['source_evidence/resources/final/manifest.json:1'])\n    references = json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())['references']\n    for reference in references:\n        claims.append(dict(claim='Literature positioning limited to consulted content: ' + reference['title'], source_ids=[reference['id']], citation_keys=[reference['citation_key']], source_locations=[reference['evidence_path']]))\n    Path('claims_grounding.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(claims=claims), indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
