{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '109,135p' paper.tex; sed -n '168,198p' source_evidence/selected/src/program.py; command -v apply_patch || true; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*validate*' -g '*scientific_evidence*' .codex | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"\\subsection{Cross-fitted local residual transfer}\nHistorical donors are partitioned into folds. For each donor fold, an auxiliary factor model is fitted without those donors. A donor's available entries among $Q$ condition that model using Equation~\\ref{eq:condition}; its finite observed target entries give residuals $e_{ij}(Q)=Y_{ij}-b^{(-i)}_{ij}(Q)$. The superscript denotes fold exclusion, not a separate fit for every donor. An unobserved donor target contributes no residual. Auxiliary predictions and the main base prediction are clipped before residual calculation or adjustment.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/src/program.py#L97-L142]]\n\nFor donor $i$, let $A_i=Q\\cap\\Omega_i$ be its shared queried anchors and $s_{ia}$ the standard deviation of column $a$ in that donor's auxiliary fit, floored at 0.025. At bandwidth $h$, the profile distance and weight are\n\\begin{equation}\n d_i^2=\\frac{\\sum_{a\\in A_i}[(Y_{ia}-y_{\\star a})/s_{ia}]^2}{\\max(|A_i|,1)},\\qquad\n w_i=\\frac{|A_i|}{|Q|}\\exp[-d_i^2/(2h^2)].\n \\label{eq:weights}\n\\end{equation}\nWeights are zero without shared anchors. For column $j$, retain only donors with finite $e_{ij}$ and positive $w_i$, denoting this set $D_j$. Compute\n\\begin{equation}\n m_j=\\operatorname{wmed}_{i\\in D_j}(e_{ij};w_i),\\quad\n n_j^{\\mathrm{eff}}=\\frac{(\\sum_{i\\in D_j}w_i)^2}{\\sum_{i\\in D_j}w_i^2},\\quad\n \\widehat y_{\\star j}=\\clip\\left(b_{\\star j}+\\alpha\\frac{n_j^{\\mathrm{eff}}}{n_j^{\\mathrm{eff}}+\\tau}m_j\\right).\n \\label{eq:correction}\n\\end{equation}\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/src/program.py#L145-L197]]\nThe weighted median is the smallest sorted residual whose cumulative weight reaches half the total. It minimizes weighted absolute residual loss, but the subsequent shrinkage and clipping mean that Equation~\\ref{eq:correction} is not generally that minimizer. A negligible total weight leaves the base unchanged. Queried entries are not residual-adjusted. Effective count measures weight concentration, not geometric support: many equally weighted distant donors can still have a large count. No extrapolation guarantee follows from this statistic.\n\n\\subsection{Historical calibration and computational scope}\nThe correction is tuned without access to the held-out new model. Historical validation rows are split into two folds. Each validation fold is excluded from both its auxiliary base fit and its nested donor bank; donors are also excluded from the fits used to obtain their residuals. Querying is simulated within each historical validation row. Absolute errors are pooled over its finite unqueried cells at the same reporting budgets, then minimized over bandwidths $\\{0.35,0.75,1.5\\}$, shrinkages $\\{4,16\\}$, and blends $\\{0,0.25,0.5,1\\}$. Ties within the implemented tolerance favor the zero blend when it attains the minimum. The final donor bank is rebuilt from history after calibration.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/src/program.py#L200-L297]]\nThis tuning target differs from the outer fixed-target loss: historical validation scores all available unqueried cells and pools cells, whereas the outer score averages row losses on sealed targets. The historical objective is a selection heuristic, not an unbiased estimate of the outer objective. There is no released outer comparison against the auxiliary unconditional-residual or direct-donor diagnostics computed during tuning.\n\nCalibration caps the pool at $\\min(512,\\max(64,\\lfloor196608/N\\rfloor))$ rows, uses at most 128 donors and 16 validation rows, and limits auxiliary ALS to 12 sweeps. These are source-defined work limits, not measured runtime claims. For $E$ observed cells, one ALS sweep has dense-solve cost $O(Er^2+(M+N)r^3)$; auxiliary fits multiply this cost. Donor residual storage is bounded by donor count times column count, and query conditioning solves a small ridge system. These algebraic costs explain CPU feasibility at this matrix scale without establishing the storage or runtime of a full upstream leaderboard acquisition.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/src/program.py#L200-L229]]\n    order = np.argsort(residuals, kind='stable')\n    sorted_residuals, sorted_weights = residuals[order], weights[order]\n    median_index = np.searchsorted(np.cumsum(sorted_weights), 0.5 * sorted_weights.sum(), side=\"left\")\n    return sorted_residuals[min(median_index, len(sorted_residuals) - 1)]\n\n\ndef _correct_target(base_prediction, residuals, target_weights, blend_strength, shrinkage_strength):\n    weight_floor = 1e-12\n    if target_weights.sum() <= weight_floor: return base_prediction\n    effective_neighbors = target_weights.sum() ** 2 / max(np.dot(target_weights, target_weights), weight_floor)\n    residual_correction = _weighted_median(residuals, target_weights)\n    correction_weight = blend_strength * effective_neighbors / (effective_neighbors + shrinkage_strength)\n    prediction = base_prediction + correction_weight * residual_correction\n    return prediction\n\n\ndef _residual_summaries(donor_residuals, neighbor_weights):\n    columns = donor_residuals.shape[1]\n    medians, effective_counts = np.zeros(columns), np.zeros(columns)\n    for target in range(columns):\n        usable = np.isfinite(donor_residuals[:, target]) & (neighbor_weights > 0)\n        target_weights = neighbor_weights[usable]\n        weight_sum = target_weights.sum()\n        if weight_sum <= 1e-12:\n            continue\n        medians[target] = _weighted_median(donor_residuals[usable, target], target_weights)\n        effective_counts[target] = weight_sum ** 2 / max(np.dot(target_weights, target_weights), 1e-12)\n    return medians, effective_counts\n\n\ndef _prepare_residual_correction(values, mask, rank, ridge, sweeps, seed):\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/__pycache__/validate_rendered_si.cpython-312.pyc\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
